# Phase 3: AI agent governance

Eventually I'd move the product higher up the value chain.

Before an agent changes code:

```text
Agent requests task
        ↓
Lore builds context package
        ↓
Known conventions
Historical decisions
Related failures
Reviewer preferences
Security constraints
        ↓
Agent writes code
        ↓
Lore evaluates result
        ↓
PR
        ↓
Human feedback
        ↓
Lore learns
```

At that point you're no longer selling "AI memory".

You're selling:

> **The organisational control plane for AI software development.**

And the timing is good. Current industry discussion is moving toward exactly this problem: as AI produces more code, verification, governance and review become increasingly important. ([TechRadar][5])

