# Business model

I would keep pricing extremely simple initially.

| Plan       |        Price | Target                         |
| ---------- | -----------: | ------------------------------ |
| Developer  |         Free | Open source / 1 developer      |
| Team       |       £49/mo | ≤5 developers                  |
| Studio     |      £149/mo | ≤20 developers                 |
| Business   |     £399+/mo | Agencies / larger teams        |
| Enterprise | £1k–£10k+/mo | SSO, audit, private deployment |

The **agency market** would be my initial target.

Not giant enterprises.

A 20-person agency might have:

```text
20 developers
30 repositories
12 clients
10 years of Git history
constant staff turnover
hundreds of undocumented decisions
multiple reviewers
multiple AI coding tools
```

That's exactly where institutional knowledge becomes painful.

And importantly, you understand that environment.

---

